    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lean heavily on **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.84) to anchor the offense today, as both benefit from favorable platoon dynamics and advantageous order positioning. **Luis Robert Jr.** is the premier play, bolstered by a significant 16% park boost that amplifies his power profile against Suarez. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.27) provides an elite start, taking advantage of a high-value platoon edge against Buehler that raises his floor well above typical projections. While **Kyle Tucker** (70.83) faces a strong matchup against Kent, he remains a high-upside play despite batting lower in the order, as his inherent talent and the opponent\u2019s vulnerable xERA profile create a favorable environment for production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the morning was keeping **Liam Hicks** (39.70) on the bench. He fell just short of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" threshold, primarily due to a 19% downgrade against Williams\u2019 pitching profile, which neutralized the gains he earned from his platoon advantage. Elsewhere, **Nasim Nunez** (41.04) and **Wade Meckler** (42.09) serve as our marginal, budget-conscious options; while their raw numbers are modest, their roles as potential stolen base contributors keep them relevant in a 5x5 Roto format where speed remains the scarcest commodity. Managers should monitor **Drake Baldwin** (48.10) closely, as his matchup against S\u00e1nchez presents a challenge; his low score is heavily dictated by the elite 2.81 xERA of the opposing starter. We are proceeding with this configuration while monitoring the status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Jacob Wilson**, who remain unavailable due to injury.",
